1. Definitions

   "Plugins" means the software published as the npm package "@threepipe/webgi-plugins", version
   1.0.0 and later, as published by the Licensor, and its source code in the
   "plugins/webgi-plugins" folder of the threepipe repository. The term covers source and compiled
   forms, with or without your modifications.

   "Application" means software or a service that you make with the Plugins and offer to its
   users: for example a website, a web, native or desktop application, a hosted service or
   viewer, an editor, a game or rendering engine, or a theme or template that end users install.
   An Application can have its own API, plugin system, scripting or embed code, and its users can
   build content and products with it.

   "Library Copy" means a copy of the Plugins, modified or not, that you offer to others to
   import, require or install into their own code, as a package, module or file.

   "Official Package" means the Plugins as the Licensor publishes them on npm.

   "You" means the person or organization that exercises rights under this license, including
   the organization you act for.

   "Licensor" means Palash Bansal and his successors and assigns.

