3. Restriction

   You must not:

   a. publish or distribute a Library Copy. Only the Licensor publishes the Official Package;
   b. include the Plugins in a library, SDK, framework or starter kit that developers install
      into their own code. Such work must declare the Official Package as a dependency and keep it
      out of its own published build. The API, plugin system or embed code of an Application is
      not such work, even when its features use the Plugins, if it does not offer the Plugins' own
      classes or modules for import;
   c. claim that you wrote or own the Plugins, or present them as your own rendering
      technology;
   d. charge for the Plugins as such. A fee for your Application, or for its features that use
      the Plugins, is allowed.

   The following are allowed:

   - an Application, for one client or for many, open or closed source, with the Plugins in any
     form (bundled, minified, tree-shaken or as separate files), served from any host or CDN that
     serves the Application, or committed as build output in your repository. Files that your
     Application loads are not a Library Copy, even at a public URL, if you do not offer them to
     others to load into their own code;
   - loading the unmodified Official Package from a public mirror of the npm registry, such as
     unpkg, jsDelivr or esm.sh;
   - a public or private fork of the threepipe repository. A package that you publish from the
     fork must not contain the Plugins;
   - a private registry, proxy or cache that serves the Official Package only to your own team;
   - unmodified copies of the Official Package, with this LICENSE file inside, in a project
     archive, container image or node_modules folder that you share;
   - not naming webgi in your product.

